<title>POLAND: Sanok to invest PLN 63.5 mln in 1997-98.</title>
<headline>Sanok to invest PLN 63.5 mln in 1997-98.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish rubber maker Stomil Sanok SA plans to invest 35 million zlotys in 1997 and 28.5 million zlotys next year, compared with 17.6 million zlotys in 1996, the firm's deputy president, Grzegorz Rysz said on Friday.</p>
<p>Rysz, speaking at a news briefing, did not give any further details. In January, the company said it planned to invest 47.1 million zlotys in 1997.</p>
<p>It has forecast to net 16.3 million zlotys in 1997, from last year's 15.1 million zlotys. Its sales are forecast to grow to 183.7 million zlotys, up from 138.5 million in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
